  <h2>Build a recommendation and a rule question</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="you should move the map" data-hint="Begin with You, add modal should, then the base verb move and its object." data-fix="You should move the map." data-success-message="Correct. Should plus the base verb gives a clear recommendation.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the recommendation</h3><p class="tile-target">A teammate thinks the map would be easier to see in another place.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="map">map</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="should">should</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">You</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="move">move</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="do i have to wear a badge" data-hint="Begin with Do, then subject I and the have-to phrase." data-fix="Do I have to wear a badge?" data-success-message="Correct. Do I have to asks whether the badge requirement applies to the speaker.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the ordinary rule question</h3><p class="tile-target">Ask whether the badge rule applies to you.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="badge">badge</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="wear">wear</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="do">Do</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three different errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="A modal connects directly to the base verb." data-fix="Visitors must show a ticket." data-why="Must takes the base verb without to." data-success-message="Correct. Must connects directly to the base verb show.">
    <h3>Drill 6: modal plus base verb</h3><p>The notice says: <span class="ex">Visitors must to show a ticket.</span> Tap the one word that must be removed.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="visitors">Visitors</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="must">must</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="show">show</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="ticket">a ticket</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="has" data-hint="After does, the main verb returns to its base form." data-fix="Does Maya have to arrive by 8:30?" data-why="Does carries present agreement, so use base have, not has." data-success-message="Correct. Does carries the tense and agreement; have returns to its base form.">
    <h3>Drill 7: question agreement</h3><p>The coordinator asks: <span class="ex">Does Maya has to arrive by 8:30?</span> Tap the word with the wrong form.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="does">Does</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="has">has</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="arrive">arrive by 8:30</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="mustn’t" data-hint="The sentence says a printed copy is optional, not prohibited." data-fix="You don’t have to print the ticket because a phone screen is fine." data-why="Don’t have to removes necessity. Mustn’t would prohibit printing." data-success-message="Correct. The available phone option makes printing unnecessary, not prohibited.">
    <h3>Drill 8: prohibition or no necessity</h3><p>The guide says: <span class="ex">You mustn’t print the ticket because a phone screen is fine.</span> Tap the phrase with the wrong meaning.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">You</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="mustn’t">mustn’t</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="print">print</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="ticket">the ticket</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="reason">because a phone screen is fine</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transforms: change meaning or time</h3>
    <p>Say each complete sentence before revealing it. Keep the stated meaning exactly.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> <span class="ex">I should move the map.</span> Change the subject to <span class="ex">she</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She should move the map.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> <span class="ex">Maya has to arrive early.</span> Ask an ordinary rule question.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Does Maya have to arrive early?</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> <span class="ex">Printing is optional.</span> Use <span class="ex">don’t have to</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You don’t have to print the ticket.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> <span class="ex">Entering is prohibited.</span> Use formal <span class="ex">must not</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Visitors must not enter.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> <span class="ex">We have to move the table today.</span> Change the time to yesterday.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We had to move the table yesterday.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> <span class="ex">A new rule begins next month.</span> Use future <span class="ex">have to</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Events will have to add a second recycling station next month.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Communicate: brief the fictional event team</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real work, school, home, location, schedule, travel, family, relationships, finances, health, legal status, rules, passwords, or future plans. Use Westbridge Community Center, invent a neutral public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask before briefing:</b> Ask the coordinator one advice question with <span class="ex">Should I...?</span> and two ordinary rule questions with <span class="ex">Do I have to...?</span>. Answer each with a reason.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a 45–60 second fictional event-team briefing.</b> Include one recommendation, two ordinary requirements, one formal firm requirement, one prohibition, one optional action, one finished past requirement, and one future requirement. Your partner identifies the status and time of each action, then asks one follow-up question.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register switch:</b> Say one requirement first as an ordinary spoken team update with <span class="ex">have to</span>, then rewrite the same requirement as a firm official notice with <span class="ex">must</span>. Explain what changed in presentation and what did not change in the underlying rule.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled recommendation, rule questions, prohibition, time, and the overlap between must and have to.">
    <h3>Five decisions with one defensible target</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="You should move the map." data-hint="The teammate gives a helpful idea, not a requirement." data-fix="You should move the map."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence presents moving the map only as a recommendation?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You should move the map.">You should move the map.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You must move the map.">You must move the map.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You have to move the map.">You have to move the map.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Do I have to wear a badge?" data-hint="Ask about an ordinary requirement with do plus have to." data-fix="Do I have to wear a badge?"><p class="quiz-question">2. Which question naturally asks in ordinary U.S. conversation whether the badge rule applies to you?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do I have to wear a badge?">Do I have to wear a badge?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Should I wear a badge?">Should I wear a badge?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do I must wear a badge?">Do I must wear a badge?</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="printing is optional" data-hint="Don’t have to removes necessity without prohibiting the action." data-fix="You don’t have to print the ticket means printing is optional."><p class="quiz-question">3. The center accepts a phone screen. What does <span class="ex">You don’t have to print the ticket</span> mean?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="printing is optional">printing is optional</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="printing is prohibited">printing is prohibited</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="printing is strongly recommended">printing is strongly recommended</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="We had to move the table yesterday." data-hint="A finished past requirement uses had to." data-fix="We had to move the table yesterday."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence accurately reports yesterday’s inspection requirement?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We had to move the table yesterday.">We had to move the table yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We musted move the table yesterday.">We musted move the table yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="We will have to move the table yesterday.">We will have to move the table yesterday.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="They can express the same rule with different framing." data-hint="Must and have to overlap; the firm notice changes register, not necessarily the underlying obligation." data-fix="They can express the same rule with different framing."><p class="quiz-question">5. A coordinator says <span class="ex">We have to lock the doors at six</span>. A posted notice says <span class="ex">Staff must lock all doors at six</span>. What is the best analysis?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They can express the same rule with different framing.">They can express the same rule with different framing.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Only the first sentence expresses a real requirement.">Only the first sentence expresses a real requirement.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Must always means the speaker invented the rule.">Must always means the speaker invented the rule.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect and retrieve</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path without looking back</h3>
    <p>How do you distinguish a recommendation, ordinary requirement, firm formal requirement, prohibition, and lack of necessity? Why can <span class="ex">must</span> and <span class="ex">have to</span> describe the same rule? What forms replace <span class="ex">must</span> for a finished past and an explicit future obligation?</p>
  </div>
